				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Update Cocoon and Sky submodules for URI robustness\n\nSynchronize the Cocoon and Sky submodules to address URI reconstruction issues across the gRPC bridge and Source Control Manager layers.\n\n**Cocoon:** Replace fragile reliance on default `.toString()` and `.external` properties with explicit structural checks for `scheme`, `authority`, and `path`. This ensures valid URI strings are constructed and transmitted to Mountain even when VS Code's URI shim varies, preventing malformed requests in document and notification flows.\n\n**Sky:** Refine URI parsing in `InstallScm.ts` to distinguish custom URI stringification from default `Object.prototype` methods. This prevents generic objects from triggering false positives during immediate service execution, aligning with the simplified bridge logic that no longer relies on retry loops.\n\nThese changes restore stability in file access, language provider invocations, and source control operations by guaranteeing accurate type handling and robust request routing.\n\nRefs: 217fc9329f143b6057295e361d30dfcf4ecda7aa (Cocoon)\nRefs: 7f22e3facc226ce9809831cf28a73e43ddf703eb (Sky)",
			"SHA": "0e9defee29e3517336ebd9e621ea6baa82c80cc3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:20:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync submodules for storage expansion, dialog fixes, and build cache stabilization\n\nSynchronize Cocoon, Mountain, and Sky submodules to their latest revisions on the Current branch to address RPC alignment, UI interaction bugs, and build stability.\n\n**Cocoon:** Introduce the `Storage.GetItems` RPC method to support bulk retrieval, expanding the interface beyond simple key-value pairs. Refactor URI resolution logic to robustly construct URL strings from `Uri` objects by explicitly checking `scheme`, `authority`, and `path` properties, preventing malformed URIs during request routing.\n\n**Mountain:** Fix `ShowMessageBox` to correctly concatenate title and detail text, restoring native dialog usability. Correct `QuickInputShowQuickPick` to preserve multi-select return arrays. Remove the obsolete `showTextDocument` handler from IPC routing to prevent redundant event dispatching now that Sky handles this natively.\n\n**Sky:** Modify `BakeExtensionManifest` to detect and invalidate cache stubs where the extension count is zero, preventing build hangs caused by stale empty records when no extensions are present.\n\nThese changes ensure robust storage handling, accurate user dialog behavior, and reliable extension metadata generation during the bootstrap sequence.",
			"SHA": "1b955092ff1986a02be27c13f186b590f2139e0d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:17:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Sky submodule to eliminate retry loops and forced UI state\n\nUpdate the Sky submodule (9c424d95 -> 14346f54) to remove aggressive retry mechanisms and forced panel manipulation from the diagnostic and tree view bridges.\n\nIn `InstallDiagnostics`, remove logic that forcibly opened the Problems panel or cleared the `activeFile` filter, allowing the `MarkersView` to manage visibility naturally based on `IMarkerService` changes. In `InstallTreeView`, strip out exponential backoff retry logic and pending attach queues, switching to synchronous execution where registration fails immediately if services are unavailable.\n\nThese changes align with the stabilized workbench bootstrap sequence, reduce bundle size, and eliminate hidden asynchronous delays and complex error-handling paths that previously masked upstream initialization timing issues.",
			"SHA": "feccffc38c954188cd9f6afab479e5965b38b94c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:12:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Sky submodule to remove aggressive retry logic\n\nUpdate the Sky submodule (9c424d95) to eliminate complex retry mechanisms and polling loops across the extension bridge layers.\n\nThe changes in `InstallInlineCompletions`, `InstallScm`, `InstallSearch`, and `InstallTreeView` replace exponential backoff and event-listener rescue paths with direct service acquisition and synchronous execution. This assumes the workbench bootstrap sequence is now stable upstream, allowing bridge layers to execute registration logic immediately. Failed registrations now fail fast rather than entering retry cycles.\n\nThis simplification reduces bundle size, removes hidden asynchronous delays in feature activation, and makes the bridge logic strictly deterministic.",
			"SHA": "7adf09f0b5b39cca2934fc5783e64941a5f9de59"
		}
